  "brief": "Array Technologies and Shoals Technologies Group are merging in an all-stock deal worth $1.1 billion, while Trian is in a takeover bid for Wendy's.\n\nArray Technologies / Shoals Technologies Group (Announced): Array Technologies and Shoals Technologies Group. Array Technologies and Shoals Technologies Group are merging in an all-stock deal [4, 6, 7]. The deal was announced by Shoals Technologies Group [1, 2, 6]. The merger agreement was signed by both companies [3, 7].\nTrian / Wendy's (Announced): Trian and Wendy's. Trian and Wendy's are in a takeover bid deal [11, 12, 13]. Wendy's has rejected Trian's takeover bid [8, 9, 10].\nSoftBank / ABB robotics business (Terminated): SoftBank's ABB Robotics Deal Blocked. SoftBank's acquisition of ABB's robotics business has been terminated [15, 16, 17]. The deal was worth $5.4 billion [15, 16, 17]. No further information is available as the deal has been terminated [15, 16, 17].\nANI Pharmaceuticals / Egetis Therapeutics (Pending approval): ANI Pharmaceuticals to Acquire Egetis Therapeutics. ANI Pharmaceuticals is acquiring Egetis Therapeutics [20, 21]. Egetis Therapeutics is selling a priority review voucher for $190 million [20]. The deal is pending approval [20, 21].\nFirst Capital, Inc. / Quantisnow (Completed): First Capital, Inc. and Quantisnow Deal. First Capital, Inc. and Quantisnow have completed their deal [22, 23]. The deal involves First Capital, Inc. expanding in Southern Indiana and Western Kentucky [22]. There is no new information on the deal [23].\nAdani Ports / Evos (Announced): Adani Ports to Acquire Evos. Adani Ports is acquiring European storage giant Evos in a €2.56 billion deal [24]. The deal is expanding Adani Ports' global footprint [24]. No further information is available [24].\nPAG / Evergrande Property Services (Announced): PAG to Acquire Evergrande Property Services. PAG is acquiring Evergrande Property Services in a HKD4bn takeover [25, 26]. The deal was announced and no further information is available [25, 26].\nTerraFlow / FlowCellutions (Announced): TerraFlow Buys FlowCellutions. TerraFlow has acquired FlowCellutions in an all-cash deal [27]. The acquisition is TerraFlow's first major move since its founding in 2021 [27]. The deal is expected to close in the first half of 2026 [27].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- QatarEnergy eyes more US LNG deals to shield supply from Mideast conflict - report [28].\n- SpaceX Stock Falls as Banks Test Demand for AI Debt [29].\n- Metairie engineering firm acquired by private equity company [30].",
